sec.p:
For control design and transient response analysis, the rotor–bearing dynamics are formulated in state-space form. A convenient approach to obtain the linearized equations of motion for the configuration shown in Fig. 2 is to select the small center-of-mass displacements x and y, along with the Euler angles α and β, as generalized coordinates, assembled in the state vector \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
