Renewable energy sources, such as solar and wind power, often produce output fluctuations that do not match with grid demand in energy-intensive systems. Flywheel energy storage systems (FESS) are employed to reduce this mismatch by smoothing power to reduce the gap between generation and consumption. Among available storage technologies, flywheels are a suitable selection and attractive due to their environmentally benign characteristics23. However, the repeated charging and discharging required by power management strategies subject the rotor to stochastic mechanical loading. The present fatigue calculation uses the nominal centrifugal stresses of an idealized, homogeneous, isotropic, constant-thickness solid disk35, as follows,24\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
